    "turn_idx": 95,
    "turn_text": "Here's what I want to say. First and foremost, the most critical thing for this nation right now is that Donald Trump went in November. And the last thing he needs is a side show, a bunch of folks auditioning for a job. He needs to be able to focus entirely on getting elected, and whatever will help him in terms of the VP pick will increase his chances and odds the greatest of winning that election. That's the outcome I want in terms of the vice presidential election process. That's certainly a compliment to find your name on these lists, but I can tell you I have no intention of engaging in speculation. I'll let the speculators do that. My job has been as going to continue to be to carry on the momentum. I'm the only member of his administration that's in the United States Senate. I have been advocating from day one of arriving there for the policies that President Trump so successfully implemented and had on the books to move forward. So President Trump knows he's got a very strong ally in me in any capacity. And right now, my focus is making certain that we are going to be ready on day one in the United States Senate to incorporate and deliver on the types of policy changes that are absolutely necessary to get our economy back, to get our national security back, to rebuild our military, and, again, have foreign relations that actually advantage America rather than every one of our adversaries. I was asking the President, literally just yesterday, who has won? under Joe Biden's policies. And the hands down winner every time you ask the question is generally China. And the next best off tend to be Iran, Russia, and all of our adversaries combined. Those are the biggest winners under Joe Biden's policy, whether it's the war he's waged on domestic energy. that essentially has allowed, you know, energy prices to go up around the world and allowed us to inadvertently fund Russia's war on Ukraine. They're refusal to impose or I should say enforce the sanctions that are on Iran. I work very hard to get those sanctions in place when I served in the Trump administration. They immediately stopped enforcing them and we saw Iran's Reserves go from single digit billions all the way up to triple digit billions under Joe Biden and they've used those funds to just basically dismantle peace in the Middle East. They funded Hamas. They fund Hezbollah. They're funding the hoodies right now, sharing down the Red Sea. Everything, every place you look, we have disasters that benefit our adversaries. Those are the only winners under the Biden administration's policy, our adversaries.",
