    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94752.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 108,
    "turn_text": "for you. Welcome back in Clay Travis Buck Sexton show. We got Senator Hagerty still with us and we kept talking during the commercial break and I wanted to give you an opportunity because we're talking to 500 stations all over the country and you were talking in the last segment about the battlegrounds in the Senate. Montana, certainly Ohio, West Virginia is looking good. But so much of this and you and I talked about this right after the 2022 disappointment. You're a data guy. People don't know this. You worked in tech. You had a business success before you came into the political arena. And you said in our conversations, we just got to dive into the data and figure out why Democrats are doing a better job getting their people out than we are. What is going to change in your mind with that data? And how can you use it to get not only for the presidential race, but in particular, in the Senate, as you mentioned, Red State, Montana, Red State, Ohio, Red State, West Virginia, and then Nevada, and Pennsylvania, and you look at that data. How do you get those voters out? What has changed since 22 based on what you've seen?",
