      },
      {
        "text": "The Boston Consulting Group has an analytically oriented culture.",
        "confidence": 0.92
      },
      {
        "text": "We conducted a post-election analysis by examining each state individually.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "Our goal was to identify the factors responsible for our loss.",
        "confidence": 0.88
      }
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      {
        "text": "Polling data is a reliable indicator of electoral outcomes.",
        "confidence": 0.93
      },
      {
        "text": "Analytical methods are appropriate for diagnosing political campaign failures.",
        "confidence": 0.91
      },
      {
        "text": "There were identifiable causes behind the unexpected loss.",
        "confidence": 0.9
      },
      {
        "text": "It is valuable to retrospectively analyze state-level performance after an election.",
        "confidence": 0.89
      },
      {
        "text": "The speaker holds credibility due to their analytical training and experience.",
        "confidence": 0.87
      },
      {
        "text": "The audience expects evidence-based explanations for electoral setbacks.",
        "confidence": 0.86
      },
      {
        "text": "A 'contrary' result implies a failure to predict accurately, which warrants investigation.",
        "confidence": 0.85
      }
    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive",
    "conversation_move_label": "Assert / Elaborate"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 94752,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94752.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 112,
    "turn_text": "And what we found, the means varied by every state, but what we found is that we were beaten on the ground. Exhibit A would be Pennsylvania. There, you had John Federman who had amassed over 900,000 early votes before he ever had to come up against Dr. Oz. Terrible debate, as you know, the most googled question in Pennsylvania for the week that followed was how do I change my vote? Well, you can't. Dr. Oz wins by 400,000 votes on election day, but that's not enough to overcome the 700,000 vote margin that Federman had. That is that sort of exhibit a to me to say we've got to have a ground game in place that's commensurate with what the Democrats have. So we have been very focused on those states where we think it's going to be close. And what we're trying to do is get low-proclivity voters. These are people that vote one, two, maybe even three out of four of the last elections, Republican voters to turn out. And the Sentinel Action Fund is the group that I've been sort of adding leadership to, but the Sentinel Action Fund has teams on the ground that are focused in states like Pennsylvania, Ohio. I mean, we will go to others, but focused on getting early ballot requests out, getting people on the absentee ballot rolls if that's what gets them to vote, requesting their early ballots if that's what's necessary and stated all depends on varying state rules. And helping people, ballot harvesting is allowed, for example, in some states, the Democrats have mastered that. We've got to play by those same set of rules, even if we don't like it. We certainly can't be caught without an ability to step up and match what the Democrats are doing. So that has been my focus. The outcome may be only a two, three, four percent difference. But in some of these states that are very close clay, that could make all the difference in the world.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_15",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Pennsylvania serves as Exhibit A for the need for a strong ground game.",
        "confidence": 0.96
      },
      {
        "text": "John Federman amassed over 900,000 early votes before facing Dr. Oz.",
        "confidence": 0.95
      },
      {
        "text": "The goal is to build a ground game commensurate with the Democrats' efforts.",
        "confidence": 0.94
      },
